" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/tuplet-swift.property":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/tuplet-swift.property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tuplet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tuplet","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV4NoteV6TupletV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"tuplet","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tuplet-swift.property","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The metronome-tuplet element, if any, using the same element structure as the time-modification element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"along with some attributes from the tuplet element.","type":"text"}]}}}